.SH "NAME"
pcre2_match_context_copy \- copy a match context
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBpcre2_match_context\fP *pcre2_match_context_copy(
      \fBpcre2_match_context\fP *\fImcontext\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function makes a new copy of a match context, using the memory
allocation function that was used for the original context. The result is \fBNULL\fP
if the memory cannot be obtained.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.